  "BWDataAcquisitionFindings": [
    {
      "goalId": "9fc800d1-92d1-5ef6-81c1-33960ae034dd",
      "verdict": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Whole goal/P requires the learner to produce their own traceable data record, not recite a model. R1 keeps all four temperature/time rows, units,source, observer, mass/volume/stirring/endpoint and missing date. R2 is a separate synthetic W3 event, not retrospective confirmation of R1;0.1C display resolution is not established uncertainty. D2 keeps raw absorbance/calibration separate from calculated concentration and preserves both dilution-history versions. These are genuine complete documentation performances for the existing EDTA/data-validity route."
    },
    {
      "goalId": "7d9fcc7f-1c20-5d5b-9cf6-05f6b624dab6",
      "verdict": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Whole P asks for an independent table/labelled graph, repeat-aware means, chemical trend reasoning, hypothesis judgment and fresh confound transfer. Dissolution time is not solubility capacity. The50C80/45s pair must both remain; spread does not justify discarding the inconvenient value or a universal extrapolation. NaCl conductivity uses mobile ions versus near-blank sucrose, and a one-sample temperature change confounds concentration inference. No actual measuring/titrating is claimed."
    },
    {
      "dependent": "4aa3a130-b517-5ac5-87b2-147fe432cadd",
      "verdict": "KEEP",
      "evidence": "Documentation9fc and interpretation7d are genuine teachers of source/condition traceability and supported data conclusions. Both new BW targets are absent before, ordinary targets after; their sequence orientation->9fc->7d->4aa is intact, including4aa requiring both. The added full capabilities are explicitly own foundations; generic BW source support is not represented as exact whole-case credit or as universal EDTA."
    }
