    "why4488Needed": "The complete4488 goal/P teaches particle/electron organization and the shared electron pair in covalent bonding, distinct from ionic/metallic models. That is the appropriate existing bond foundation for a donated shared pair.",
    "why04faNeeded": "The complete04fa goal/P teaches electron loss/gain and donor/acceptor roles. It supports rejecting the specific false inference that a coordinate-bond arrow automatically meansCu(II)->Cu(I). Pair donation to a shared bond is not full free-electron transfer.",
    "whyEPA9b56IsNotUniversalPrior": "Its whole P assesses VSEPR domains, shapes, simple angles and lone-pair angle changes. The unchanged363c P explicitly supplies a qualitative bond fragment and suitable occupied donor/unoccupied acceptor orbitals, while denying any complete geometry or all-emptyCu(II)d-shell conclusion. It demands no angle prediction or full coordination geometry; that performance is not universal prerequisite evidence.",
    "whyPractical973cIsNotUniversalPrior": "Its whole P requires supervised carbonyl assay execution with controls and own observations, plus mixture selectivity limits. The unchanged363c goal/P interprets coordination in the supplied Fehling context, tartrate-solubilisedCu(II), model donor availability and coordination/redox distinction. It does not perform that assay or require an independent aldehyde/ketone identification. Full practical973c is therefore not a universal predecessor for this different capability.",
    "methodOwnedContentRetained": "363c itself still teaches and assesses occupied ligand donor versus suitable empty acceptor, purpose of tartrate,Cu(II) coordination versus laterCu(I) inCu2O, fresh O-pair versus stipulated C-H-without-donor comparison, and limits of fragments. No expectation is erased, moved to an unassessed hint or replaced by a lower goal.",
    "oldTopicsAndPracticalDutiesRetained": "All existing EPA/carbonyl/alcohol targets, roles, whole profiles and actual execution requirements remain. Their removal from this one prerequisites list neither declares them noncurricular nor credits their mastery.",
    "unchangedPriorHoldBoundary": "Own18-FIRST remains exact for its old363c prerequisites. This separate scientific successor changes that relation on the above content grounds; it does not rewrite that prior conditional HOLD or waive a genuine practical obligation."
  },
